{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 11, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie begins with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, as a harvard undergraduate who is trying to find his place in the world. after a painful breakup with his girlfriend, erica, mark creates a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive.\n\nthe site becomes a huge success, but also generates a lot of controversy and gets mark into trouble with the university administration. this leads to mark being approached by a group of students, including twins cameron and tyler winklevoss, who ask him to create a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. mark agrees, but soon becomes obsessed with the project and begins to work on it with his friend eduardo saverin, played by andrew garfield.\n\nas the site, which mark calls \"the facebook\", begins to gain popularity, mark and eduardo's friendship begins to fray. mark becomes increasingly obsessed with the site and starts to push eduardo out of the project. meanwhile, the winklevoss twins become suspicious of mark's intentions and begin to accuse him of stealing their idea.\n\nthe movie then jumps back and forth between the story of facebook's creation and the subsequent lawsuits that mark faces. the film portrays mark as a complex and often unlikeable character, who is driven by a desire for recognition and acceptance. the supporting cast, including justin timberlake as sean parker, the co-founder of napster, and rooney mara as erica, mark's girlfriend, all give strong performances.\n\none of the standout aspects of the film is the script, written by aaron sorkin. the dialogue is witty and fast-paced, and the characters are all well-developed and complex. the film also features a great 